From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:25:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 121/342] meson_vdec: the S905's video decoder (VDEC_1),
 MPEG-1/2 bring-up

A driver for the Amlogic GXBB video decoder, published as
video/meson_vdec/0 (headers/private/drivers/meson_vdec.h): it powers
VDEC_1 up, loads the AMRISC firmware the caller hands in, sets up the
VIFIFO ring and the stream parser, gives the firmware eight NV12 frames
(two canvases each, from canvas 0x80 on), feeds the elementary stream
through the parser with its 00 00 01 FF marker, and hands out the
frames the firmware reports until the caller gives them back.

Written from facts read from Linux's GPL staging driver (register
names, offsets, values and their order; no code), in the port's
docs/m26-vdec-facts.md. The interrupts are rising edges that the GIC
takes as levels, so every wait also polls the registers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
