+/*
+ * Copyright 2026, haiku-odroid-c2 port authors.
+ * Distributed under the terms of the MIT License.
+ *
+ * meson_vdec: the Amlogic S905's (Meson GXBB) video decoder, VDEC_1, for
+ * MPEG-1/2 so far, as video/meson_vdec/0 (headers/private/drivers/
+ * meson_vdec.h).
+ *
+ * The decoder is an AMRISC processor running Amlogic's firmware, which the
+ * caller hands in. The elementary stream goes through the stream parser
+ * (ESPARSER) into a ring in memory (the VIFIFO) that the decoder reads; it
+ * decodes into eight NV12 frames, each two canvases, and reports each
+ * decoded frame in a scratch register with a mailbox interrupt. The
+ * register facts are in the port's docs/m26-vdec-facts.md.
+ *
+ * Both interrupts are rising edges, which the GIC takes as levels here, so
+ * every wait also looks at the registers itself every few milliseconds.
+ */
+
